# The Rails API in server/ is deployed separately (Render/Fly/Railway), never on
# Vercel. Excluding it keeps the frontend deployment small and guarantees Vercel
# never tries to interpret its Ruby files.
#
# This is belt-and-braces: the directory used to be called api/, which is a magic
# path on Vercel - every file under a root-level api/ becomes a Serverless
# Function, and with a Ruby runtime available all 34 .rb files were picked up,
# blowing past the Hobby plan's 12-function limit and failing the build.
server/

# Local-only files that never belong in a deployment.
*.log
